 35CL    32S(A,P)                      2019SE09,1973GO16         ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+32}S ground state.                                        
 35CL c  2019Se09: a 21-MeV |a beam was produced from the 10-MV FN tandem Van de
 35CL2c  Graaff accelerator at Triangle Universities Nuclear Laboratory (TUNL). 
 35CL3c  Targets were 15.9-|mg/cm{+2} {+nat}S in cadmium sulfide and            
 35CL4c  46.3-|mg/cm{+2} {+nat}S in antimony sulfide. Reaction products were    
 35CL5c  momentum-analyzed by the TUNL high-resolution Enge split-pole magnetic 
 35CL6c  spectrograph and detected using a high-resolution position-sensitive   
 35CL7c  focal-plane detector consisting of two position-sensitive gas avalanche
 35CL8c  counters: a gas proportionality energy loss section and a residual     
 35CL9c  energy scintillator (FWHM=24 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q), at |q=10|' to
 35CLAc  50|'. Deduced levels, J, |p from one-step finite range triton transfer 
 35CLBc  FRESCO-DWBA analysis. Deduced the thermonuclear {+34}S(p,|g){+35}Cl    
 35CLCc  reaction rate via Monte Carlo methods.                                 
 35CL c  1973Go16: 19.991-, 20.025- and 20.284-MeV |a beams were produced from  
 35CL2c  the University of Notre Dame FN tandem Van de Graaff accelerator.      
 35CL3c  Natural sulfur targets were prepared by vacuum evaporation of CdS onto 
 35CL4c  20-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backings. Protons were analyzed with broad-range  
 35CL5c  magnetic spectrographs at 15|', 30|', 70|', 90|', and 120|' and        
 35CL6c  detected using nuclear track plates at the focal planes. Measured      
 35CL7c  |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced 102 levels.                                      
 35CL c  1971Au07: a 28.8-MeV |a beam of 0.1-0.5 |mA was produced from the Naval
 35CL2c  Research Laboratory (NRL) isochronous cyclotron. The target was made by
 35CL3c  evaporating natural PbS onto a 30-|mg/cm{+2} carbon backing, and the   
 35CL4c  effective {+32}S thickness was 163 |mg/cm{+2}. Protons were detected   
 35CL5c  using two counter telescopes with FWHM=250 keV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). 
 35CL6c  Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and J-dependence for the g.s. and  
 35CL7c  1763-keV level from local zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis of the        
 35CL8c  measured |s(|q).                                                       
